{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>the land of Havilah where there is gold</b> — to explain that this is not the Havilah of Egypt, of which it says, \"and they dwelt from Havilah to Shur\" (Genesis 25:18), for this one is east of the east. And he further mentioned the bdolach there, in praise of the river, for in the sand that is in it and along its bank will be found that good gold and the bdolach and the shoham stone, for thus it is found in rivers — in some of them gold is found there, and in others silver is found in them, and likewise bdolach and precious stones are found mostly in rivers. And according to the opinion of the early authorities (Rashi and Saadiah Gaon, and likewise it is found in Zohar, Chayei Sarah 125), \"Pishon\" is the Nile of Egypt; it surrounds all this land of Havilah and comes from there over the face of all the land of Egypt until it falls into the Great Sea at Alexandria of Egypt."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Ramban cites Rashi and Saadiah Gaon by epithet; the parenthetical source references appear in the Hebrew text and are rendered as they stand."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:23:54.438376028Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}